sequenceDiagram
    participant Officer as Authority Officer (browser)
    participant TARA as TARA (RIA OIDC OP)
    participant UI as Gate Authority UI
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (<gateId>)
    participant Auth as AccessChecker
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Route as Business Route

    Note over Officer,TARA: Step 1 — TARA OIDC login (out-of-band of the gate's REST API).<br/>Officer authenticates with Estonian eID / Mobile-ID / Smart-ID;<br/>TARA returns an ID Token (RS256-signed JWT, claims: iss, aud,<br/>sub=Estonian PIC, resource_access.efti-gate.roles, subsets,<br/>efti.scope, exp, jti).

    Officer->>+TARA: OIDC authorize / authenticate
    TARA-->>-Officer: ID Token (JWT)

    Note over Officer,UI: Step 2 — UI bearer-attaches the JWT to subsequent gate calls.

    Officer->>+UI: Search "123ABC"
    UI->>+Gate: GET /v1/identifiers/123ABC<br/>Authorization: Bearer <TARA-JWT>

    Gate->>+Auth: authenticate(request)
    Auth->>Auth: Validate JWT signature against cached JWKS<br/>(fetched from TARA_OIDC_DISCOVERY_URL)
    Auth->>Auth: Validate iss == TARA, aud == TARA_CLIENT_ID, exp > NOW()
    Auth->>+DB: Check sessions denylist for the JWT's jti
    DB-->>-Auth: not revoked
    Auth->>+DB: Resolve the latest active users row by tara_sub = jwt.sub;<br/>verify jwt.iat ≥ users.token_revoked_at
    DB-->>-Auth: User{id='d2e3f4a5-…', is_active=TRUE, roles={'AUTHORITY':['<authorityA>']}, subsets=['EU07'], token_revoked_at=NULL}

    Note over Auth: Permission claims are read from the resolved users row,<br/>NOT directly from the JWT — TARA's `resource_access` may<br/>differ from the gate's `users.roles` if admin has updated<br/>scope since the JWT was issued. JWT carries identity<br/>(`sub`) and freshness (`iat`, `jti`); the gate carries the authorisation.<br/><br/>Missing-row policy: if no active users row matches the JWT `sub`,<br/>respond 401 TOKEN_INVALID with detail "no provisioned user".<br/>Admin must POST /api/v1/users first.<br/><br/>Per-user broadcast revocation: if jwt.iat < users.token_revoked_at,<br/>respond 401 TOKEN_INVALID with detail "token revoked".

    Auth-->>-Gate: AuthenticatedUser{<br/>userId="d2e3f4a5-…", roles=["AUTHORITY"],<br/>scope=["<authorityA>"], subsets=["EU07"], jti="abc..." }

    Gate->>+Route: handle(exchange, user)
    Note over Route: @Access(AUTHORITY) — user.roles contains AUTHORITY → OK
    Route->>Route: authorityId = user.scope.first() = "<authorityA>"
    Route->>Route: subsetCheck: requested ⊆ user.subsets → OK
    Route->>Route: Execute identifier search (latest-row resolution per dataset_id)
    Route-->>-Gate: result
    Gate-->>-UI: 200 OK (SSE stream)
    UI-->>-Officer: Search results

    alt Invalid JWT signature / expired / aud mismatch
        Officer->>Gate: GET /v1/identifiers/123ABC<br/>Authorization: Bearer <bad-jwt>
        Gate->>Auth: authenticate
        Auth-->>Gate: null (signature/exp/aud invalid)
        Gate-->>Officer: 401 Unauthorized<br/>{"code":"TOKEN_INVALID"}
    end

    alt JWT in denylist (per-token revocation via /api/v1/auth/logout)
        Officer->>Gate: GET /v1/identifiers/123ABC<br/>Authorization: Bearer <revoked-jwt>
        Gate->>Auth: authenticate
        Auth->>DB: Check sessions denylist for the JWT's jti
        DB-->>Auth: present (revoked)
        Auth-->>Gate: null
        Gate-->>Officer: 401 Unauthorized<br/>{"code":"TOKEN_INVALID","detail":"Token has been revoked"}
    end

    alt User-level revocation (per-user broadcast via /api/v1/users/{id}/revoke-token)
        Officer->>Gate: GET /v1/identifiers/123ABC<br/>Authorization: Bearer <jwt issued before revoke-token>
        Gate->>Auth: authenticate
        Auth->>DB: Resolve users row; jwt.iat < users.token_revoked_at
        DB-->>Auth: User{token_revoked_at=2026-04-23T10:00:00Z}
        Auth-->>Gate: null
        Gate-->>Officer: 401 Unauthorized<br/>{"code":"TOKEN_INVALID","detail":"Token has been revoked"}
    end

    alt Valid JWT but wrong role
        Officer->>Gate: GET /api/v1/gates (admin endpoint)<br/>Authorization: Bearer <authority-only-jwt>
        Gate->>Auth: authenticate → AuthenticatedUser{roles=["AUTHORITY"]}
        Gate->>Route: @Access(ADMIN) — user.roles ∌ ADMIN → fails
        Gate-->>Officer: 403 Forbidden<br/>{"code":"FORBIDDEN"}
    end

    alt Authority requests subset outside scope
        Officer->>Gate: GET /v1/dataset/...?subsetId=EU03 (user.subsets=["EU07"])
        Gate->>Auth: authenticate → ok
        Gate->>Route: subsetCheck: ["EU03"] ⊄ ["EU07"] → fails
        Gate-->>Officer: 403 Forbidden<br/>{"code":"FORBIDDEN_SUBSET"}
    end
